; Open struct-map (loose CBOR "rest row") FLATTENED-JSON end-to-end vectors.
; The captured rest entries render at the SAME JSON object level as the declared fields (serde
; flatten), and read back symmetrically (declared field names bind first, every other key -> rest).
; --json-serde-derives --json-schema-export, --wasm=false (the wasm rest surface is registered
; separately). See tests/open-struct-map-json-e2e/tests.rs for the value-level vectors.
foo = { 1: uint, 2: text, * uint => any }   ; uint key domain, any value
baz = { 1: uint, * any => any }             ; any key domain, complex keys error on to_json
typed = { 1: uint, * uint => text }         ; fully-typed rest (no any anywhere)
dupp = { 1: uint, * uint => any ; @duplicates preserve
}                                           ; PairMap twin: actual duplicate keys error on to_json
dupt = { 1: uint, * uint => text ; @duplicates preserve
}                                           ; TYPED PairMap twin of `typed`: same flattened JSON,
                                            ; so the same JSON Schema (schema-parity vector)

; ---- TYPED key domains (`* K => V` where K is not bare uint/text/any) ----
; A typed rest key images through the `any` domain's convention applied to K's OWN CBOR bytes (text
; verbatim, uint/nint decimal, everything else a loud to_json error), and reads back numeric-first
; with a FALLBACK to the text reading when K refuses the numeric one. The four key rules below pin
; that convention against the four things K can admit: both readings, text only, uint only, and a
; bounded text (refinement on read).
; the metadatum-shaped union: admits BOTH readings
md = int / bytes / text
; TEXT-only K (the fallback clause's vector). `@newtype` takes an optional accessor name, so it must
; be the last thing on its line — a trailing comment after it is read as that name.
tk = text ; @newtype
; UINT-only K (both-readings-refused error, and the schema anti-vector)
uk = uint ; @newtype
; BOUNDED K: an out-of-bounds member name is a parse error, never a capture
bt = text .size (1 .. 4) ; @newtype

tkk = { 1: uint, * md => md }                 ; typed K, typed V: values ride V's OWN serde
tkkp = { 1: uint, * md => md ; @duplicates preserve
}                                             ; PairMap twin of `tkk` (schema-parity + duplicates)
tonly = { 1: uint, * tk => uint }
uonly = { 1: uint, * uk => uint }
bonly = { 1: uint, * bt => uint }

; A PRIMITIVE typed K (`.size` keeps it off the peeked path) states its image directly instead of
; round-tripping through CBOR, and a `bytes` K has no member-name image at all — its flattened region
; is a pure error surface in both directions. Both routes are compiled here, not only snapshotted.
pk = { 1: uint, * uint .size 1 => uint }
bk = { 1: uint, * bytes => uint }
